okay one more story having to do with  joe manchin killing the build back  better legislation this week we have to  talk about how the squad was actually  proven right and centrist democrats were  proven wrong at least when it comes to  one important aspect of all this a few  weeks ago when the physical  infrastructure deal was being debated  there were several members of congress  the progressive democrats specifically  who urged house speaker nancy pelosi and  senate majority leader chuck schumer to  couple the infrastructure deal with the  multi-trillion dollar spending bill  built back better and indeed for a few  weeks those two bills were coupled  together and the idea was that manchin  and some of these other centrist  democrats they're sure yeses on physical  infrastructure they definitely want to  see that get passed but when it comes to  the multi-trillion dollar spending plan  we just can't trust them they they seem  to be changing their minds and you know  we just don't know if they're sure yeses  eventually nancy pelosi decided to cave  to the moderates in the party and uh  they decided to separate the two bills  and biden gave her the stamp of approval  to do so saying that we're going to be  able to assure that joe manchin is going  to vote yes on both pieces of  legislation so  joe biden he essentially gave us his  word on that but the squad they weren't  buying it so when it came time to  actually vote on the infrastructure deal  in november most of the congressional  progressive caucus they decided to vote  yes that's pramila jayapal katie porter  rokhana and a bunch of other familiar  names but the squid the six squad  members they held firm and they voted no  that's jamal bowman corey bush  alexandria ocasio-cortez ilhan omar  ayana presley and rashida talib and they  voted no not because they don't want to  see infrastructure get passed that's  actually quite the opposite they  definitely are in support of revamping  american infrastructure but they viewed  this as the best bargaining chip that  they had for making sure that both of  the bills got past the physical  infrastructure and the so-called human  infrastructure  and at the time there was a sentiment  among many democrats that was like look  let's get infrastructure done biden  hasn't had a significant legislative  achievement in a while maybe not since  the coveted stimulus plan was passed  back in march and we also don't know if  we're going to be able to in the long  term maintain this 60 vote threshold  that we need in the senate to get this  passed because you really can't trust  republicans like maybe they'll decide  they don't want to support this thing  anymore the idea was let's get it done  now we'll get this round of positive  press coverage about the infrastructure  deal and then before the end of the year  we'll get build back better done through  budget reconciliation and that will  prompt another round of positive media  coverage and it'll be viewed as yet  another accomplishment for joe biden and  the democrats obviously that didn't play  out and the squad was right to question  manchin's willingness to go along with  the rest of the party we actually have a  video now of camila jayapal talking to  many hassan about everything that went  on and she maintains that she has no  regrets in all of this but i i sort of  doubt that let's take a look at the  video and then we'll come back how do  you feel about that today do you feel  that joe biden let you down and do you  feel you got played by joe manchin  no and no um we are you know for the  weeks and the days going up to the vote  in the house everybody every day if i  had counted i would be if i got a penny  for every time somebody said to me this  is not going to happen you all have  given up everything we got it done in  the house now i am in the same place in  saying that we are getting grenades  rolled at us all the time we have to  pick them up we have to put the pin back  in and we have to continue to focus on  the fact that this is going to be rocky  we can't hang our you know our  commitments and our hopes on the words  of one senator or two senators we have  to continue to work to get it done and  the vast majority of it is done and so i  was on the phone with uh senator schumer  today with the white house and i believe  we will still get it done it's gonna be  rocky and we just have to continue to  leave no space in the um in the  commitment to getting it done and listen  the president's word is on the line here  and i do still believe that he is going  to do what he told me and what he told  our caucus and what he told the country  he would do  had we not done what we had done  and if he doesn't congresswoman  what was that  and if he doesn't  no we're gonna do it we're gonna do it  and the leverage that you had your  critics would argue was lost when you  voted for biff i just wonder do you  regret voting for the biff deal now in  hindsight given it's now months later  and joe manchin is nowhere closer to  signing off on 1.75 trillion  no i don't regret it because i i think  our leverage was at the maximum point on  the other side of the coin we have one  of the squad members aoc tweeting about  this saying quote when a handful of us  in the house warned this would happen if  democratic leaders gave manchin  everything he wanted first by moving  biff that's the bipartisan  infrastructure framework before build  back better instead of passing together  many ridiculed our position maybe  they'll believe us next time or maybe  people will just keep calling us naive  and unfortunately given the  establishment democrats track record on  all this and when it comes to them  trying to listen to progressives it'll  probably be the second one of those two  options there uh and they'll probably  just keep getting called naive but there  is a counter argument to all of this  that we have to consider as well and it  is a strong one which is that even if  the entire progressive caucus held firm  and they prevented the infrastructure  deal from getting passed in the house  and they made sure that it was only  going to happen in one piece of  legislation the two bills had to be put  together and that was it are we sure  that joe manchin would have actually  voted for it like the argument is that  he would right because he supports the  infrastructure deal and west virginia  desperately needs new infrastructure but  he just as easily could have done the  same exact thing here he could have said  you know i like some pieces of this  legislation i like the infrastructure  stuff but there are members of my party  who are trying to poison pill it with  all this other nonsense and there was  this opportunity to make this bill  bipartisan and the progressives are  ruining that opportunity so i just can't  support this bill in any form that also  could have happened that also is a  legitimate possibility and then  progressives at the end of the day they  look bad because they are the ones who  are blamed for not allowing  infrastructure to pass when even some  centrist republicans are willing to do  it and you have the remainder of the  democratic party in support of it so  what we know for now is that the squad  was definitely right not to trust joe  manchin not to trust his word because  his word means nothing but whether or  not we actually would have been able to  get both of these things passed by the  end of the year that remains uncertain  and to be honest i guess we'll never  truly know it's sort of unfalsifiable in  a sense because it really just comes  down to what joe manchin is thinking on  any particular day and that's  unfortunately what we have to deal with  so that's everything having to do with  buildback better as of now we're going  to go to a break back after this
 

